From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wmvcore: The metadata editor (6515)

WMCreateEditor was a stub. The editor opens an ASF file's header: the
Content Description Object (Title, Author, Copyright, Description,
Rating) and the Extended Content Description Object become the
attributes of its IWMHeaderInfo3 (the writer's attribute store). Flush
writes the two objects back, keeping the header's other objects and
the data after it, and updates the file size; Close without Flush
drops the changes.
---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
index 6c0e96f..dacead6 100644
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/Makefile.in
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@ EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
 SOURCES = \
 	async_reader.c \
+	editor.c \
 	profile.c \
 	profile_xml.c \
 	version.rc \
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/editor.c b/dlls/wmvcore/editor.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..fe3a985
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/editor.c
@@ -0,0 +1,626 @@
+/*
+ * The metadata editor (WMCreateEditor)
+ *
+ * Copyright 2026 Stained Glass OS contributors
+ *
